[center][size=7][b]Sell Me Slave! (SMS)[/b][/size]
[size=5][b][color=#FFD700]🌟 BIG AI UPDATE (v2.0.0) 🌟[/color][/b][/size]
[b][color=#00ff00]STATUS: OFFICIAL RELEASE[/color][/b][/center]

[center][size=5][b]Important: SMS uses a single-module setup with optional MCM bridge support for easy configuration.[/b][/size]
[size=5][b]Full Turkish (TR) and English (EN) localization is supported.[/b][/size][/center]

[line]

[size=6][b]What Does This Mod Do?[/b][/size]

Sell Me Slave! (SMS) adds a brand new dynamic to Mount & Blade II: Bannerlord: [b]The Underground Prisoner Trade[/b]. Visit the backstreets of any town to find the Captive Trading area, or intercept Lords directly on the campaign map to buy their prisoners. Through a seamless, native-like trade interface, you can purchase regular prisoner troops to bolster your ranks or buy out high-value captive Heroes from across Calradia — all with real consequences.

[line]

[size=6][b]🚀 BIG AI UPDATE (v2.0.0) Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]🤖 Autonomous AI Slave Traders:[/b] AI Lords are no longer excluded from the dark side of Calradia! Lords with low honor will now actively participate in the underground slave trade. They will periodically visit the backstreets to purchase troop slaves to bolster their ranks, and even purchase enemy noble prisoners from other lords!
[*][b]🗣️ Rumour Has It Integration:[/b] Seamless integration with our other mods. If you have [i]Rumour Has It[/i] installed, AI slave trading activity will generate tavern gossip, revealing the dirty secrets of "honorable" lords.
[/list]

[line]

[size=6][b]Core Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Native Trade UI Integration:[/b] Seamlessly buy prisoners using the native party screen with dynamic bottom-panel cost calculations.
[*][b]Captive Trading (Towns):[/b] Visit town backstreets to access randomized prisoner pools. Lower-tier troops are common, while elite units are rare.
[*][b]Buy Captive Heroes:[/b] Buy captive Lords from across the realm. They are not teleported; they will be physically delivered to your party based on distance!
[*][b]Map Encounters:[/b] Illegal trading isn't limited to towns. Talk to any Lord on the map to negotiate for their prisoners.
[*][b]Prisoner Exchange (Cartel):[/b] Negotiate prisoner swaps with Lords — exchange your captives for theirs.
[*][b]Moral & Social Consequences:[/b] Every transaction has weight. Gain [b]Roguery XP[/b] and [b]Relationship[/b] with the seller, but suffer [b]Honor loss[/b] and a rising [b]Criminal Rating[/b].
[*][b]Deterministic Pricing:[/b] Prices are stable per game day, preventing menu-flickering. Based on tier, skills, and equipment.
[*][b]Localization:[/b] Full English and Turkish support included.
[/list]

[line]

[size=6][b]Underground Consequences[/b][/size]

Human trafficking is highly illegal in Calradia (unless you're a bandit).

[list]
[*][b]Crime Rating:[/b] Buying slaves increases your criminal rating with the local faction.
[*][b]Honor Loss:[/b] Trading in human lives is dishonorable. Your Honor trait will decrease proportionally to the gold spent.
[*][b]Roguery XP:[/b] You gain Roguery experience for every successful illegal transaction, with real-time UI notifications.
[*][b]Social Gains:[/b] Illegal gold is still gold! Lords will like you more for providing them with "off-the-record" funding.
[/list]

[line]

[size=6][b]Configuration Modes[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]JSON Mode (Default):[/b] Works without any dependencies. Settings are read from [font=Courier New]config.json[/font].
[*][b]MCM Mode (Optional):[/b] If you have MCM installed, sliders appear automatically within the same [font=Courier New]SellMeSlave[/font] module. No separate downloads required.
[/list]

Configurable settings include: Lord Transit Time, Lord Escape Chance, Price Multipliers (common & lord), Crime Rating Penalty, Relation Gain, Roguery XP Scale, Honor Loss Scale, and AI Slave Trade chances.

[line]

[size=6][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download the latest package and extract it to your Bannerlord [font=Courier New]Modules[/font] folder.
[*]Enable [font=Courier New]SellMeSlave[/font] in the launcher.
[*][b]Load Order:[/b] Place SMS after official modules and framework mods.
[/list]

[line]

[size=6][b]FAQ[/b][/size]

[b]Q: How do I access the trader?[/b]
A: In towns, go to "Go to the backstreet" and select [b]"Captive Trading"[/b]. On the map, talk to a Lord and look for the new trade dialogue option.

[b]Q: Why don't I see certain Lords in the buy list?[/b]
A: The mod correctly filters out Heroes held by your own party or clan to prevent "buying from yourself".

[b]Q: Do I need MCM?[/b]
A: No, it's optional. The mod works fine with default settings or manual JSON edits.

[b]Q: Is it safe to add mid-save?[/b]
A: Yes. It is perfectly safe to add to an existing campaign.

[b]Q: What happens if a purchased Lord dies during transit?[/b]
A: You will receive a full gold refund with a notification.

